def source_html(rows):return ''.join('<div class="source" id="source-'+i+'"><b>'+i+' · '+org+'</b><a href="'+url+'">'+title+'</a><p>'+desc+'</p></div>' for i,org,title,url,desc in rows)
page('APPENDIX A · RESEARCH','Sources and research boundaries',lead('Primary sources reviewed on September 13, 2026. Dynamic prices and product offers should be rechecked before using a comparison in a customer quotation.')+source_html(sources[:5])+note('Market estimates in this plan are carefully separated: official broad-market context, explicit serviceable-pool hypotheses, and a bottom-up acquisition model. No purchased prospect dataset, independent customer survey, or verified OverHead sales ledger was available.'))
page('APPENDIX A · RESEARCH','Cost and operating references',source_html(sources[5:])+'''
<h2>Method</h2><p>The review combined current local product materials, release artifacts, public website availability, and primary-source market and pricing research. It did not change the product or attempt a live payment. Product claims were checked against implementation and release evidence, and prior positioning materials were treated as company statements rather than independent traction evidence.</p>
<p class="small">The financial model is original scenario analysis. Competitor descriptions are limited comparisons drawn from official pages, not exhaustive product reviews. No external source is used to validate OverHead’s modeled conversion, acquisition cost, retention, valuation, or projected revenue.</p>
''')

page('APPENDIX B · PRODUCT EVIDENCE','Review record and supporting materials',lead('This plan reflects the inspected OverHead project and public product surfaces as of September 13, 2026.')+table(['Reference','Evidence and use'],[['<span id="source-P1">P1 · Product and pricing</span>','website-next/app/data.js; business-foundation.js; investors/page.jsx; live homepage. Supports product positioning, published tiers, and commercial scope.'],['<span id="source-P2">P2 · Implementation</span>','package.json version 0.3.12; electron-backend.cjs; src/App.jsx. Reviewed customer work, account controls, synchronization, storage, and billing references. Source evidence is not independent performance testing.'],['<span id="source-P3">P3 · Commercial readiness</span>','docs/production-readiness.md; stripe-server-readiness.md; release-notes-0.3.12.md; functions/index.js. Supports the billing, signing, trial, refund, and paid activation gates.'],['<span id="source-P4">P4 · Business principles</span>','docs/business-principles.md and website business foundation. Supports owner control, progressive adoption, evidence/recovery, and accurate commercial claims.'],['<span id="source-P5">P5 · User guide and screenshot</span>','docs/user-guide-content.mjs; scripts/capture-guide-images.cjs; published user guide. Dashboard capture uses a fictional local sample profile.'],['<span id="source-P6">P6 · Availability / artifact checks</span>','HTTP 200 for homepage, investor page, user guide, and desktop 0.3.12 ZIP (application/zip). Configured billing endpoint returned 404. Local 0.3.12 installer Authenticode status: NotSigned.'],['<span id="source-M1">M1 · Financial model</span>','Companion financial-model.json, monthly CSV, formula workbook, and model.py. Original scenario inputs and calculations; no historical financial statements incorporated.']],'compact')+'''
<h2>Public product references</h2><p><a href="https://overhead-office.web.app/">Product website</a> · <a href="https://overhead-office.web.app/user-guide/">Illustrated user guide</a> · <a href="https://overhead-office.web.app/investors/">Existing business / investor overview</a></p>
<h2>Owner-supplied information</h2><p>The owner confirmed <b>Overhead LLC</b> as the business name and DBA and requested a general-purpose plan. Formation jurisdiction, address, ownership percentages, headcount, historical revenue, customer count, and desired financing amount were not supplied. The plan does not invent them.</p>
<h2>Refresh schedule</h2><p>Update readiness after paid launch, customer metrics after each cohort review, projections quarterly, and competitor/vendor prices before formal distribution. Preserve this edition as the dated planning baseline.</p>
''')

